### ============================================================================
### SECTION 2: Show all registrations — GET /api/registrations
### ============================================================================

### Case 14: Default list (200 OK, page: 1, pageSize: 10, totalCount >= 25)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 15: Newest first (200 OK, registrations sorted newest first)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 16: Second page, custom size (200 OK, page: 2, pageSize: 5)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

### Case 17: Page past the end (200 OK, items: [], totalCount unchanged)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=999
Accept: application/json

### Case 18: Invalid page (400 Bad Request, errors.Page)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=0
Accept: application/json

### Case 19: Page size too large (400 Bad Request, errors.PageSize)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 3: Find by type, status and participant name — GET /api/registrations?...
### ============================================================================

### Case 20: Find by type (200 OK, all VIP)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=VIP
Accept: application/json

### Case 21: Find by status (200 OK, all Confirmed)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed
Accept: application/json

### Case 22: Find by participant name (200 OK, contains 'juan')
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 23: Name search ignores case (200 OK, same items as Case 22)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN
Accept: application/json

### Case 24: Partial name match (200 OK, contains 'dela')
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela
Accept: application/json

### Case 25: Combined filters (200 OK, type=Competitor & status=Pending & participantName=juan)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 26: No matches (200 OK, items: [], totalCount: 0, totalPages: 0)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz
Accept: application/json

### Case 27: Invalid type (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor
Accept: application/json

### Case 28: Invalid status (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Done
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 4: Find registration by ID — GET /api/registrations/{id}
### ============================================================================

### Case 29: Existing ID (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/{{sampleId}}
Accept: application/json

### Case 30: ID that does not exist (404 Not Found, Registration.NotFound)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### Case 31: Not a valid GUID (404 Not Found via route constraint)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/abc
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 5: KPI summary — GET /api/registrations/summary
### ============================================================================

### Case 32: Summary returns all fields (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 33: Status counts add up (confirmed + checkedIn + pending + cancelled = totalRegistrations)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 34: Totals match the list (totalRegistrations = totalCount from GET /api/registrations)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 35: Money adds up (totalFees - totalPayments = uncollectedPayments)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 36: Cancelled are excluded from money (Compare seeded cancelled CS27-0023, CS27-0024, CS27-0025)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Cancelled
Accept: application/json

### Case 37: Summary updates after a new registration
# Step 1: Note current summary
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 37 (Step 2): Post new registration (Exhibitor, fee 1500, paid 500)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1037",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 500.00
}

### Case 37 (Step 3): Verify summary updated (+1 total, +1 pending, +1500 fee, +500 paid, +1000 uncollected)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 38: /summary is not treated as an ID ({id:guid} constraint ensures 200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 6: Database persistence — SQLite
### ============================================================================

### Case 39: Data survives a restart (Check total count before and after restart)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 40: Unique indexes exist in SQLite database
# Verified by inspection of carshow.db schema / SQLite indexes:
# IX_Registrations_PlateNumber (UNIQUE) and IX_Registrations_RegistrationNumber (UNIQUE)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=1&pageSize=1
Accept: application/json
